        <+ [Credit flattened demand]: demand fell much less steeply with price when credit was available for the bednet
            {fidelity: "quotation", pinpoint: "p. 35", note: "Tarozzi et al. 2011, rural Orissa, India, outside the ten: 52 percent bought on credit at full price, against 96 percent take-up when nets were free. The bulletin flags that microfinance clients are a different population.", causes: {from: fee, to: takeup, sign: "-", basis: study, given: ["credit was available for the bednet"]}}
        <- [People may discount future costs]: it is also possible that people put less emphasis on costs in the future (in this case, loan repayments) #conceded
            {fidelity: "quotation", pinpoint: "p. 36", note: "A rival reading of the credit result, present bias rather than lack of cash.", causes: {from: fee, to: takeup, sign: "-", basis: asserted, hedged: true, given: ["credit was available for the bednet"], how: {actor: household, situation: "costs that fall in the future (in this case, loan repayments)", habit: "put less emphasis on costs in the future", response: "buys on credit"}}}
